## Why This Is Asked
Tests knowledge of extending behavior without modifying core code (Open/Closed). It also assesses choosing a clean extension point (Strategy) and a simple registry to map runtime options to implementations.

## Key Concepts
- Strategy pattern
- Registry/Factory
- Open/Closed principle
- Dependency injection

## Code Example
```javascript
class Serializer {
  serialize(record) { throw new Error('Not implemented'); }
}
class JSONLSerializer extends Serializer {
  serialize(record) { return JSON.stringify(record) + '\n'; }
}
class CSVSerializer extends Serializer {
  serialize(record) { /* minimal CSV escaping omitted for brevity */ return Object.values(record).join(','); }
}
class NDJSONSerializer extends Serializer {
  serialize(record) { return JSON.stringify(record) + '\n'; }
}
```

```javascript
// Registry / factory
const Registry = {
  jsonl: () => new JSONLSerializer(),
  csv: () => new CSVSerializer(),
  ndjson: () => new NDJSONSerializer()
};

function createWriter(format) {
  const serializer = Registry[format]?.();
  if (!serializer) throw new Error('Unknown format');
  return {
    write: (record) => serializer.serialize(record)
  };
}
```

